From 366fb704c5e90d88c855be1067a370819f283a3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crindo18 <chrisjohnalado@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 11:44:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] M6 GUI, shared plots, and a manifest-identity guard for
 s08

GUI (Objective 4): src/gui/HimigTransformApp.m - load/record/play,
waveform, spectrogram with constellation overlay, offset histogram,
ranked candidates, live baseline<->enhanced toggle, match-time readout
and an accept/reject lamp.

Built programmatically on uifigure rather than as a .mlapp: a .mlapp is
a binary container that Git cannot merge, cannot diff and cannot review,
and it costs a lost afternoon the first time two people open it. This
uses the same components App Designer emits, so it is the same MATLAB
app in a reviewable form. Indexes load lazily and cache, so cold start
stays inside the 30 s budget with the ~72 MB enhanced index. Microphone
failures are caught and shown in the status line rather than thrown -
the Load File path always works (risk R11).

Implemented plotConstellation and plotOffsetHistogram, shared by the GUI
and the paper figures so both render identically.

s08 guard: matching queryIDs are NOT sufficient. queryID is assigned
sequentially as buildQueryManifest walks the catalogue, so removing the
duplicate holdout song and rebuilding renumbered everything after it.
Two result files can then share a queryID that refers to different
audio, and McNemar would silently pair a 3 s clean query against a 10 s
query at -20 dB with no visible symptom. s08 now verifies songID,
lengthSec, targetSnrDb and noiseType agree row for row and refuses to
proceed otherwise.
